<Base title="Data policy">
  <h2>Data flow</h2>
  <p>
    The community surface is a thin read-side over snapshots produced by the
    Trace Commons server. The pipeline:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>Contributor's local Ironclaw captures and scrubs a trace, then queues it.</li>
    <li>Ironclaw uploads the scrubbed envelope to the hosted ingest API.</li>
    <li>Server applies two gates: a <strong>novelty</strong> gate (is this record genuinely different from everything already filed?) and a <strong>substance</strong> gate (is this substantive work, not template-shaped filler?). Both must pass.</li>
    <li>Accepted submissions are signed, filed into the register, and recorded in the credit ledger.</li>
    <li>A snapshot worker computes leaderboard rows + corpus aggregates on a schedule, applying min-cell and noise guards.</li>
    <li>This site renders against the latest snapshot.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Consent scopes</h2>
  <p>
    Consent scopes are the access mechanism, not only a privacy control. They are how
    a contributor — rather than an operator or a buyer — decides what the register may
    be used for. Nothing exceeds the scope a record was given, and scopes can be
    withdrawn.
  </p>
  <p>
    The contributor's standing policy carries a <code>consent_scope</code> that
    determines which uses the envelope contents permit:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>debugging_evaluation</code> (default): debugging, evaluation, aggregate analytics.</li>
    <li><code>benchmark_only</code>: evaluation, benchmark generation, aggregate analytics.</li>
    <li><code>ranking_training</code>: + ranker training.</li>
    <li><code>model_training</code>: + training-data inclusion.</li>
    <li><code>public_attribution</code>: separate, profile-management consent that links the contributor's pseudonym to a public handle. Does NOT grant any trace-content uses on its own.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Aggregation guards</h2>
  <p>
    The snapshot worker honours three operator-tunable guards:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>TRACE_COMMONS_ANALYTICS_MIN_CELL_COUNT</code> — a leaderboard row is suppressed if the contributor's window count is below this threshold.</li>
    <li><code>TRACE_COMMONS_ANALYTICS_BROAD_RELEASE_NOISE</code> — Laplace noise on every aggregate count.</li>
    <li><code>TRACE_COMMONS_ANALYTICS_BROAD_RELEASE_PRIVACY_ACCOUNTING</code> — budget tracking across snapshots.</li>
  </ul>

